    science: "Cleveland Clinic notes that oxytocin plays a role in behaviours such as trust, romantic attachment and parent–infant bonding, and that its levels increase with hugging and orgasm; researchers are still studying its roles (Cleveland Clinic, “Oxytocin”).",
