    science: "The Harvard Study of Adult Development, begun in 1938, found that close relationships, more than money or fame, keep people happy throughout their lives and are better predictors of long and happy lives than social class, IQ or even genes (Harvard Gazette, 2017).",
    scienceUrl: "https://news.harvard.edu/gazette/story/2017/04/over-nearly-80-years-harvard-study-has-been-showing-how-to-live-a-healthy-and-happy-life/"
