    why: "God designed order so that life could flourish, and some forms of ordered difference (parents and young children, teachers and learners, the experienced and the new) help love do its work. Scripture says God “is not a God of confusion, but of peace” (1 Cor 14:33). But the gospel radically reshapes hierarchy: in Christ “there is neither Jew nor Greek, slave nor free, male and female” (Gal 3:28), and the greatest is the servant of all (Mark 10:43-44).",
